package entity

// pettaunthate.go — an enchanter's pet's taunt gives 70% of the threat it gave (the GM Jibwiz's
// petition 1928, 2026-11-13: "Reduce the agro generated by enchanters Grand animation and other
// enchanter pet line pets via their taunt by 30%").
//
// A pet's taunt (pet.go petTauntLocked: the Grand Animation and any enchanter's pet with no template
// row; pettemplate.go petTemplateTauntLocked: the "pet animation" template's animations and golems,
// Gymon's Animation, the Earthen and Ferrous Golems) raises the pet's threat on its target to one above
// the top and lands a hit, whose damage is hate as any hit's. For a pet an enchanter summoned
// (petState.enchanter, a merc enchanter's too), all the threat the taunt added, the raise and its
// hit's, is cut to enchanterPetTauntHatePct of it, and the creature chooses its enemy again from its
// list (pickEnemyLocked): the pet no longer always lands on top, it takes the creature only when its
// threat after the taunt is the highest. The magician's earth pets' taunts, a charmed creature's and a
// merc's own are as they were; a training dummy's hate is its own (dummy.go) and a Metal Moogie keeps to
// his challenger, so neither is cut.
const enchanterPetTauntHatePct = 70

// petTauntHateCutLocked takes the pet's threat on t before its taunt and returns what cuts the threat
// the taunt added (the file's doc), to run after it (a defer). Nothing for a pet no enchanter
// summoned, a dummy or a Metal Moogie's duel. Must be called with the lock held.
func (w *World) petTauntHateCutLocked(ps *petState, t *NPC) func() {
	if !ps.enchanter || ps.npc.Charm != nil || t.Dummy != NotDummy || t.challenge != nil {
		return func() {}
	}
	id := ps.npc.ServerID
	before := t.Threats[id]
	return func() {
		after, ok := t.Threats[id]
		if t.Dead || !ok || after <= before {
			return
		}
		t.Threats[id] = before + pctOf(after-before, enchanterPetTauntHatePct)
		if e := w.pickEnemyLocked(t); e != 0 {
			t.CurrentEnemy = e
		}
	}
}
